# SiteGround auto-deploy

Production: **https://www.mogenas.com** via `npm run deploy` (rsync over SSH `mogenas-siteground`).

## Required behavior

After you **create or edit any deployable file**, run deploy **in the same turn** before finishing — do not wait for the user to ask:

```bash
cd "/Users/mihalenasi/Developer/mogenas.com corpo page" && npm run deploy
```

**Deployable files:** `index.html`, `assets/**`, `*/index.html` (legal pages), `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`, `.htaccess`

**Skip deploy** only when changes are limited to: `.env`, `.cursor/**`, `scripts/**`, `package.json`, `.gitignore`, docs-only files, or the user says not to deploy.

## On success

Briefly confirm: deployed to SiteGround and live at https://www.mogenas.com/

## On failure

Report the error (SSH, rsync, path). Do not claim the site is updated. Suggest `npm run setup-ssh` if the key is not loaded.

## Do not

- Commit or push to git unless the user asks
- Commit `.env` or SSH keys
